# Tree-construction vectors the HTML tree builder does not pass yet, one per line:
#
#   <file>#<n> TAB <stage> TAB <what> TAB <reason>
#
# The id is the file in third_party/html/wpt/html/syntax/parsing/resources and the vector's
# position in it, from 1. The stage is the one that will remove the line: 3e (foreign content,
# the fragment parsing algorithm). Stage 3d (the table insertion modes, template) is done and
# has no line left; the vectors that were 3d and also hold svg or math stop in 3e now, and say
# so in their reason ("was 3d").
# tools/conformance/html_tree_suite.py fails the gate on a vector that fails and is not
# listed, on a listed one that now passes or stops somewhere else (a stale entry), and on
# the size of the file only through the floor on how many vectors pass. The list is
# generated by `html_tree_suite.py --propose` from where the tree builder stops
# (GTEXT_HTML_TREE_E_NOT_YET names the construct), never from a wrong tree: a vector that
# parses to the wrong tree is a failure and cannot be listed.
#
# One kind is not a stage: `none dom` (five columns, the last locking the first difference).
# The four webkit02.dat vectors that put a `selectedcontent` in a `select` expect the
# element to hold a copy of the selected option's content. That is a DOM behaviour of the
# form controls (the "select" chapter's selectedcontent steps, run when an option is
# inserted), not a step of the tree construction chapter, which does not mention the
# element; no tree builder that follows the chapter builds it.

